1
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:10,550
Good morning.

2
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:12,260
Good morning. My name is Richard Stewart.

3
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:13,950
I'm here to see Mr. Carlson.

4
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:18,100
Please  sit down,Mr.Stewart.  Mr. Carlson will be with you shortly.

5
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:22,080
Thank you.

6
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,360
Excuse me, Mr. Carlson,

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,660
but Richard Stewart is here

8
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:27,620
for his ten o'clock appointment with you.

9
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:29,040
OK. Thank you.

10
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:31,410
Like I said, he'll be with you shortly.

11
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:37,650
Thank you.

12
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:42,130
Yes, Mr. Carlson. Yes, sir.

13
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:44,180
He's ready for you, Mr. Stewart.

14
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,480
Thank you. In there?

15
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,840
Yes. In there. Good luck.

16
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:58,340
Come in, come in.

17
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:00,510
This is a crazy morning. Hello, Richard.

18
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:01,610
Hello, Mr. Carlson.

19
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:03,570
Sit down, sit down.

20
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:05,900
Thank you for seeing me on such short notice.

21
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,210
I hope you've brought your pictures along.

22
00:01:08,210 --> 00:01:13,230
I see that you have. Let's get right to it.

23
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:15,560
We need a new coffee-table book,

24
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:20,550
and a book of photos about the United States still feels right.

25
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:28,570
OK, let's take a look.

26
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:43,310
Good. Very good. Family Album, U.S.A.

27
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:45,870
It's an excellent title.

28
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:48,370
If you had to describe the book in one sentence,

29
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:50,430
how would you do it?

30
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:56,180
Well, I'd describe it as a book which is a ...

31
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:58,540
a portrait of the United States--

32
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:02,880
the places, the people--mostly the people.

33
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:05,530
The things they do, the ways they live,

34
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:09,270
the places they visit, and the landmarks.

35
00:02:09,270 --> 00:02:12,280
A photographic journey.

36
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,300
These are wonderful--

37
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,980
these photos in your performing arts section.

38
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,480
Carnegie Hall, Lincoln Center.

39
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:20,030
I'm glad you like them.

40
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:23,740
I do, but ...

41
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:25,810
But?

42
00:02:25,810 --> 00:02:30,000
There's something missing. You've got a good eye, Richard.

43
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,980
You're a terrific photographer.

44
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:34,900
But before I can publish your work,

45
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,980
I need to meet with my marketing department,

46
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:41,000
and you've got to do one more thing.

47
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,190
What's that, Mr. Carlson?

48
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:44,930
In the section on culture,

49
00:02:44,930 --> 00:02:46,970
you've included performing arts centers,

50
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:50,710
but you've left out street performance. The mimes.

51
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:56,910
The musicians. The dancers--in the parks and on the streets.

52
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:59,890
Richard, if you go out    Richard,

53
00:02:59,890 --> 00:03:01,440
and photograph street performances in the city,

54
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,540
you'll have it.

55
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:06,080
That is a great idea.

56
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:09,440
The performing arts centers and the street performances.

57
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,750
I'll do it.

58
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:14,430
If you do it, I'll publish your work.

59
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:15,690
Are you serious?

60
00:03:15,690 --> 00:03:17,520
I've never been more serious.

61
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:22,000
When do you think you can return with street performances?

62
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,170
A couple of weeks.

63
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:28,550
If they're as good as the rest of these pictures, it's a deal.

64
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:35,060
You won't be disappointed, Mr. Carlson. Thanks.

65
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:37,510
Good-bye, Richard, and good luck. See you in two weeks.

66
00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:43,680
Good-bye, Mr. Carlson. Thanks.

67
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:47,690
So if you like the street-performance photos,

68
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:50,540
you'll really publish Family Album, U.S.A.?

69
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:53,530
When I say something, I mean it.

70
00:03:53,530 --> 00:03:55,370
Go to work. Good-bye.

71
00:03:55,370 --> 00:03:58,370
Good-bye.
